  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (0.00) and model shows persistent overestimation.",
    "Correct for lagged underestimation in early forecast periods — especially when true values rise after a dip.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in price — model tends to overreact and overcorrect.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction: if forecast deviates > ±5% from recent 7-day average, adjust toward it.",
    "Increase downward bias in 30-day forecasts when sentiment is flat (0.00) and historical volatility is low.",
    "When sentiment is positive (0.50), allow slight upward bias but cap forecast at 10% above recent 14-day high to avoid overextension."
